  "id": "a2d21c5b-568e-544a-90ad-699b8cede168",
  "slug": "lazy-cheeseburger-kebabs-recipe-11961969",
  "name": "Lazy Cheeseburger Kebabs",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Chef John's cheeseburger kebabs are made with ground beef and Cheddar, wrapped in lavash flatbread, then skewered and baked. \"This easy technique is usually applied to Middle Eastern flavors, but this cheeseburger version, especially drizzled with my secret secret sauce, is a familiar flavor you won't want to miss.\"",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C). Line a rimmed baking sheet with foil."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add beef to a bowl, and evenly apply the salt, pepper, cayenne, and cheese to the top. Use a fork to gently mix and fold everything together until evenly combined."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Lay lavash bread on a cutting board, with the shorter 8-inch side facing you. Dampen fingers and transfer meat onto the lavash. Spread as evenly as possible, all the way to the edges, except leave 1 inch uncovered at the top of the sheet, furthest away from you."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Once the meat is spread evenly, gently press the meat near the far edge to cover the rest of the sheet in a thinner layer, smearing it thinly to the edge. Starting from the edge closest to you, roll the bread up tightly and evenly, finishing with the seam at the bottom."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Use a serrated knife to cut the roll in half. Then slice each half evenly into 4 pieces. Line the 4 pieces up with the seams trapped in the center and carefully push 2 skewers through the 4 rolls to secure and form the kebab."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Transfer kebabs to the prepared baking sheet with the best looking sides facing up. Brush with the butter, turn over, and brush the other side. Space kebabs a couple inches apart."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 7 minutes. Turn the kebabs over, and turn on the oven\u2019s broiler."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Broil kebabs until nicely browned and the meat is cooked through, 2 to 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "For secret secret sauce, whisk mayonnaise, Dijon mustard, ketchup, and buttermilk together in a small bowl until smooth. Taste, and adjust any ingredients to your taste."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "Serve kebabs with your favorite cheeseburger accompaniments, drizzled with the secret, secret sauce."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 2,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
